# SafetyNet Landing - Agent Guide

This file is the repo-wide operating guide for Codex and other coding agents.
It applies to the canonical SafetyNet landing repo and its sibling worktrees.

## Repository Layout

The durable project folder is:

`C:\Users\CampbellMcCord\repos\Safetynet\Safetynet-landing`

That outer folder is not itself the git repo. The canonical repo is:

`C:\Users\CampbellMcCord\repos\Safetynet\Safetynet-landing\safetynet-landing`

Sibling worktrees may also exist:

- `safetynet-landing-preparer` - preparer worktree for drafting, editing, and building implementation tasks.
- `safetynet-landing-reviewer` - reviewer worktree for validation and critique tasks.

The worktree path is the operating boundary. Do not edit sibling worktrees unless the user explicitly assigns you to that worktree.

## Default Edit Policy

- Use canonical `safetynet-landing` on `main` for repo-wide policy and documentation work unless instructed otherwise.
- Use `safetynet-landing-preparer` for preparer implementation tasks.
- Use `safetynet-landing-reviewer` only for reviewer validation tasks.
- Do not switch branches in the canonical repo while another agent is active in a worktree.
- Before staging or committing, run `git status --short --branch` and stage only files belonging to the current task.

## Dirty Worktree Policy

- Run `git status --short --branch` before making edits.
- If the worktree is dirty, identify whether existing changes overlap the task.
- If existing changes overlap the files you need to edit, pause and summarize the situation before proceeding.
- Never revert, overwrite, or clean up changes you did not make unless the user explicitly approves it.
- If canonical `main` is behind remote, note it before real implementation work and avoid merging or rebasing without user direction.

## Handoff Policy

`HANDOFF.md` is required for tasks performed in the preparer worktree only.

Canonical audits, plans, and small repo-policy documentation changes do not require `HANDOFF.md` unless the user asks for one.

When a preparer task requires handoff, use this structure:

```text
TASK
[What was asked]

DONE
[What was executed - specific, not summary]

SKIPPED / REJECTED
[Anything not done and why - none if not applicable]

QUALITY GATES
[Gate name]: PASS / FAIL

OPEN FOR REVIEWER
[Anything requiring reviewer judgment - none if not applicable]

BRANCH
[Branch name and commit reference]
```

## Project Commands

- `npm run build:css` - compile Tailwind from `styles/input.css` to `styles/tailwind.css`.
- `node build-faqs.js` - bake `data/faq.json` into `index.html`.
- `npm test` - run Jest tests.
- `npx playwright test` - run Playwright smoke tests.
- `npm run lint` - run ESLint checks.

Known command caveat: `package.json` sets `"type": "module"`, while `build-faqs.js` currently uses CommonJS `require`. Verify or fix that path before relying on `node build-faqs.js` for production work.

## Known Caveats

- The outer `Safetynet-landing` folder is a container, not the git repo.
- Canonical `main` may be dirty or behind `origin/main`; check before editing.
- Existing `CLAUDE.md` contains useful worktree rules, but its preparer-role section is stale or overbroad when read from the canonical repo.
- `CLAUDE.md` remains unchanged for now; reconciling or replacing it is a separate cleanup task.
